QNX 8 has O_BINARY/O_TEXT but no setmode(): make it a no-op.

QNX's <fcntl.h> defines O_BINARY and O_TEXT (both 0), so io.c compiles
its DOS text/binary mode switching, which calls setmode(). QNX 8's libc
has no setmode() (unix.h no longer declares it): libruby failed to link.
Both modes are the same on QNX, so setmode() is a no-op that reports
binary mode.

Upstream-Status: QNX-specific

--- a/io.c
+++ b/io.c
@@ -58,6 +58,10 @@
 
 #ifdef __QNXNTO__
 #include <unix.h>
+/* QNX defines O_BINARY and O_TEXT (both 0: there is no text mode), so the
+ * DOS-style code below is compiled in, but QNX 8's libc has no setmode().
+ * With no difference between the modes, switching is a no-op. */
+#define setmode(fd, mode) ((void)(fd), (void)(mode), O_BINARY)
 #endif
 
 #include <sys/types.h>
